Gingham and GinghamICU (the "Software") are distributed as binary frameworks.
This license lets you use them; it doesn't sell them or give you their source.

1. Free use. You may use the Software, free of charge, in any app or tool,
   personal or commercial, free or paid, public or internal, and ship it to
   your users as part of your app (inside its bundle). Without a license key
   a table of the Software shows up to 10,000 rows of its data source and a
   notice that more need a license key.

2. License keys. A license key, bought from the copyright holder or given by
   them, removes the row limit for the apps (bundle identifiers) and the
   major version of the Software it names. Keys are sold per developer: each
   person who writes or debugs code that uses the Software in a licensed app
   needs one. A key for a major version (for example 1.x) covers every
   release of that major version, and apps shipped with it stay licensed
   when the key's term ends. Trial keys work until the day they name. The
   terms of a key beyond this license are those agreed when it is bought.

3. Restrictions. You may not:
   a. circumvent, disable or change the row limit or the license key check,
      or help others do it;
   b. share or publish a license key except inside the apps it is for;
   c. distribute the Software on its own, or as part of a library, framework,
      SDK, component or tool for other developers, rather than of an app for
      its users;
   d. decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse engineer the Software,
      except as far as the law where you are allows it despite this term;
   e. remove or change the Software's copyright notices.

4. Third-party software. GinghamICU contains ICU (Unicode License V3) and code
   of swift-foundation-icu (Apache License 2.0), which stay under their own
   licenses: see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Ship those notices with an app that
   uses GinghamICU.

5. Termination. If you break this license, it ends for you, and so do the
   license keys you hold, unless you put things right within 30 days of being
   told about it.

6. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind, express or implied, including the warranties of merchantability,
   fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

7. Limitation of liability. In no event shall the copyright holder be liable
   for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in an action of
   contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in connection with the
   Software or its use, beyond the amount you paid for your license keys in
   the twelve months before the claim.

